{"step_index":1251,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:40:10Z","thinking":"**Examining Set Difference Cardinality**\n\nThe initial understanding was incorrect; the lemma `Finset.card_sdiff` does not require a subset hypothesis, the more general formula applies directly: `(t \\ s).card = t.card - (s ∩ t).card`. A different lemma, such as `Finset.card_sdiff_of_subset` likely applies. Considering an application of `Finset.card_sdiff` leads to evaluating `(Finset.univ \\ s).card = Finset.card Finset.univ - (s ∩ Finset.univ).card`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > scratch_goal.lean\nimport Mathlib\n\nexample {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (s : Finset V) :\n    Fintype.card V = s.card + (Finset.univ \\ s).card := by\n  have h_diff : (Finset.univ \\ s).card = (Finset.univ : Finset V).card - (s ∩ Finset.univ).card := Finset.card_sdiff\n  rw [Finset.inter_univ, Finset.card_univ] at h_diff\n  have h_le : s.card ≤ Fintype.card V := by\n    have hsub : s ⊆ Finset.univ := Finset.subset_univ _\n    have hcard := Finset.card_le_card hsub\n    rw [Finset.card_univ] at hcard\n    exact hcard\n  omega\nEOF\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch_goal.lean\n","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing card split lemma","toolSummary":"Check card split in scratch_goal.lean"}}]}
