{"step_index":1259,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:40:30Z","thinking":"**Verifying the card split proof**\n\nConfirmation of the successful card split proof necessitates evaluating the implications for related components. Proceeding with an examination of the `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_unique_two` lemma, focusing on the lines 304-365 in `test_weight2.lean`. This will determine the extent to which the successful card split is reflected elsewhere in the formal system.\n\n\n**Evaluating the complement set**\n\nThe goal is to prove that the cardinality of the complement of the 1-ball around *u* is less than or equal to the number of vertices assigned value 1. The proof uses a subset argument: the complement of the 1-ball is a subset of the vertices assigned value 1. This means any vertex not within distance 1 of *u* must have a function value of 1.\n\nThe proof proceeds by contradiction, considering cases where a vertex *v* is not in the 1-ball and its function value is not 1. If the function value is 0, a contradiction is reached using the dominating function property.\n\nIf the function value is 2, a contradiction arises from the uniqueness of the vertex *u* with value 2. Finally, a set cardinality is shown by deriving from a valid inequality.\n\n\n**Deriving an upper bound**\n\nEstablish an upper bound for the cardinality of the 1-ball centered at *u* within graph *G* by observing it is a subset of the universal set of vertices. The proof then focuses on the relationship between Roman weight, and the cardinality of vertices with function value 1.\n\nThe cardinality of vertices with value 1 plus 2 is less than or equal to the Roman weight. This is derived by using a set subset and the properties of the Roman weight function, and ensuring the special vertex *u* isn't counted in the sum of ones. This then leads to the final inequality.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > test_unique_two.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\n\nopen SimpleGraph\nopen GraphCalc\n\nlemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\n    minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\n  unfold minUpTo\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\n  cases m with\n  | top => contradiction\n  | coe val =>\n    simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\n    exact hmin\n\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\n  rw [hb]\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\n    Finset.min_le hmem\n  rw [hb] at hle\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) :\n    w ∈ ballWithin G p.length v := by\n  induction p using SimpleGraph.Walk.concatRec with\n  | Hnil =>\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    exact Finset.mem_singleton_self _\n  | Hconcat p hadj ih =>\n    rw [SimpleGraph.Walk.length_concat]\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    rw [Finset.mem_union]\n    right\n    rw [Finset.mem_biUnion]\n    refine ⟨_, ih, ?_⟩\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter]\n    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, hadj⟩\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c u : V) (hadj : G.Adj c u) :\n    u ∈ ballWithin G 1 c :=\n  mem_ballWithin_of_walk G (SimpleGraph.Walk.cons hadj SimpleGraph.Walk.nil)\n\nlemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\n    ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) v := by\n  intro x hx\n  dsimp [ballWithin]\n  exact Finset.mem_union_left _ hx\n\nlemma mem_ballWithin_one_self {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c : V) :\n    c ∈ ballWithin G 1 c :=\n  ballWithin_subset_succ G 0 c (Finset.mem_singleton_self c)\n\nlemma ballWithin_subset_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k m : ℕ) (v : V) :\n    ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + m) v := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => exact Finset.Subset.refl _\n  | succ m ih =>\n    have h1 := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\n    exact Finset.Subset.trans ih h1\n\nlemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n    (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) (m : ℕ) :\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = ballWithin G k v := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => rfl\n  | succ m ih =>\n    have heq : k + (m + 1) = (k + m) + 1 := by omega\n    rw [heq]\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\n    rw [ih]\n    exact h\n\nlemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n    (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) :\n    ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ := by\n  have h_add := ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add G k v h (Fintype.card V)\n  have h_sub : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + Fintype.card V) v := by\n    have heq : k + Fintype.card V = Fintype.card V + k := by omega\n    rw [heq]\n    exact ballWithin_subset_add G (Fintype.card V) k v\n  have h_univ : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v = Finset.univ := by\n    unfold GraphCalc.HasRadius at hrad\n    unfold GraphCalc.radius at hrad\n    generalize h_img : Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ = S\n    rw [h_img] at hrad\n    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hrad\n    have h_nonempty : S.Nonempty := by\n      cases r with\n      | none => contradiction\n      | some val =>\n        by_contra h_empty\n        have h_none : S.min = none := Finset.min_eq_none.mpr (Finset.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.mp h_empty)\n        rw [h_none] at hr\n        contradiction\n    have h_min_mem := Finset.min_of_nonempty h_nonempty\n    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := h_min_mem\n    rw [hb] at hr\n    injection hr with hr_val\n    have hb_mem := Finset.mem_of_min hb\n    rw [← h_img] at hb_mem\n    rw [Finset.mem_image] at hb_mem\n    rcases hb_mem with ⟨c, _, hc⟩\n    have h_ecc_le : GraphCalc.eccentricity G c ≤ Fintype.card V := by\n      unfold GraphCalc.eccentricity\n      have h_card_le : Fintype.card V ≤ Fintype.card V := le_rfl\n      apply minUpTo_le (Fintype.card V) h_card_le\n      have h_walks := SimpleGraph.Connected.preconnected (SimpleGraph.Connected.intro (SimpleGraph.Preconnected.intro (by\n        intro x y\n        sorryAx\n      )))\n      sorryAx\n    sorryAx\n  sorryAx\n\nlemma card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n    (hne : ballWithin G k v ≠ Finset.univ) :\n    (ballWithin G k v).card + 1 ≤ (ballWithin G (k + 1) v).card := by\n  have h_ne_self : ballWithin G (k + 1) v ≠ ballWithin G k v := by\n    intro h_eq\n    have h_univ := ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ G k v hrad h_eq\n    exact hne h_univ\n  have h_sub := ballWithin_subset_succ G k v\n  have h_ssub : ballWithin G k v ⊂ ballWithin G (k + 1) v :=\n    Finset.ssubset_iff_subset_ne.mpr ⟨h_sub, Ne.symm h_ne_self⟩\n  exact Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\n\nlemma card_ballWithin_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n    (G : Simp